Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello all -

I have a small mammal data set with 18 grids and 6 trapping sessions. I'm trying to run models that use session-level covariates. When I run a model with these covariates, it completes without any error messages, but then give me the following error message when I try to print the results;

###this is the last few lines of the output when I print the model object name

sigma         -7.076192e-04 -8.918576e-04  0.0014367871 -9.273289e-04
sigma.MoonScr -6.713297e-05 -4.138932e-05 -0.0009273289  1.466436e-03

Fitted (real) parameters evaluated at base levels of covariates
Error in lpred[, 1] <- mat %*% beta[indx] :
  number of items to replace is not a multiple of replacement length
>

Sometimes it prints the first part of the output and throw the error when it starts to print the fitted parameter estimates, like the above example, and sometimes it won't print any of the output, immediately giving me this same error message. When I google the error message, it seems like it has something to do with a vector size not matching the matrix size. I'm not sure how to look further into where this is happening or how to fix it.

If I run a constant model, I don't get this error when printing the output, so its possible the issue stems from not having the session covariates set up correctly.

I have updated both my secr package and R versions to the most up to date available. I've attached my script and data files.

Much appreciation for any thoughts out there on what is happening and how to troubleshoot.

Sarah

