Hi Sarah
I haven't reviewed what we did before, so this may be confusing, but...
You need to give each 'session' its own appropriate 'traps' object, rather than attempting to use a common traps object across all sessions. Then the 'usage' for a session-specific traps object will have just 3 columns, not 18, and in fact you may not need 'usage' at all if traps were used/notused for whole sessions. I can't provide code right now, maybe later. [I also note that the 'provisional' version of 'secr' has a bug in read.traps that complains when the markocc argument is NULL - will fix that very soon].
Murray

