Hi SECR users,

I have a pretty long lists of models to run, and I am looking for a way to make it more efficient (I've already read the Speed Tips:)).

I found the function par.secr.fit, and I see it as a way to run models on few cores, as well as running models one by one without having me to start them (so I can leave the PC for a night and have an owsome morning ;)).

Yet, I faced a problem that i cannot over ride... ;/

Following the example (http://rpackages.ianhowson.com/cran/secr/man/par.secr.fit.html) I am running following code:

#model1, g0 constant
model1 <- list(capthist = "all_years", group = "sex", model = list(g0 ~ 1), CL = FALSE)
#model2, g0 differing between sexes
model2 <- list(capthist = "all_years", group = "sex", model = list(g0 ~ g), CL = FALSE)

fit <- par.secr.fit (c(model1,model2), ncores = 2)

But I am getting error:

Error in checkForRemoteErrors(val) :
  2 nodes produced errors; first error: nie znaleziono obiektu 'all_years'
In addition: Warning messages:
1: In x$trace <- trace : Coercing LHS to a list
